title: False-AUTOFOLD gate result — auto-fold safety is conditional on in-graph dependency linkage
summary: |-
  Ran Jinx's false-AUTOFOLD ship-gate as a characterization-test corpus of genuine cross-symbol semantic conflicts through consolidate(). The result refines Jinx's hypothesis into a mechanistic rule: the engine catches a cross-symbol semantic conflict IFF a dependency path links the conflicting symbols in the lifted graph (Merkle-by-target essence propagation moves the dependent's essence on both sides → knot). It is BLIND to conflicts between independent symbols and across extern/cross-file boundaries. Dependency-linked 3/3 caught, unlinked 5/5 blind, overall false-CLEAN 5/8 (63%).</summary>
