learnings:
  - 'Auto-fold safety is CONDITIONAL: the engine catches a cross-symbol semantic conflict iff a dependency path links the symbols in-graph (Merkle-by-target propagation) — NOT a blanket blindness'
  - The blind spot is precisely independent symbols + cross-file/extern composition (cross-file refs are extern free-refs, never local edges, so no Merkle link)
  - 'Phase C admission rule falls out directly: auto-admit only dependency-connected WEFTs; independent/cross-file-spanning WEFTs need human/peer confirm — a graph-reachability check on the existing edge graph'
  - 'Same double-tax bug: CAUGHT same-file, BLIND cross-file — the local-edge-vs-extern-ref distinction is the whole hinge'
